        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-01T23:13:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See the Note in this section: https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/guides/dts/api-usage.html#node-identifiers\n\nWhen using the DT macros, all non-alphanumeric characters are converted to \u0027_\u0027 and the name is converted to lower case.",
      "parentUuid": "ec0eb569_01a87108",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 204,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 204,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "81574cb1bc2432812cbba70b33961fbc22c6fe72",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "602da58a_114d11f1",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/drivers/overlay.dts",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 204,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-01T23:21:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Yep, you need to also change DT_DRV_COMPAT but confusingly the \"-\" changes to \"_\"\n\nI figured there was something like that, but I grepped for pi3usb9201-emul, didn\u0027t find anything, and gave up. Not really a fan of APIs that involve defining macros that you never directly use, either, but I guess that\u0027s the Zephyr way.\n\nNow that it builds with the -emul, should I have that or go back to just syv682x?",
      "parentUuid": "78807c86_d4cc80ad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 204,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 204,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "81574cb1bc2432812cbba70b33961fbc22c6fe72",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
